## Best Nail Shapes for Simple Fall Designs

Almond and squoval are the two best nail shapes for simple fall designs, because both give a clean line for polish to sit against without the sharp corners that show early wear. Almond elongates the finger and suits solid color especially well, while squoval reads slightly more relaxed and pairs naturally with two-step designs like a French tip.

Squoval is a blend of square and oval, built by softening the corners of a square tip into a gentle curve rather than a hard right angle. It solves a real complaint people have with fully square nails, which is that sharp corners catch on everything and chip first, while still keeping enough flat nail bed for a crisp French tip line. <a href='/blog/fall-nails/fall-almond-nails'>Fall almond nails</a> take that same low-maintenance logic further, since the tapered tip means less flat surface area to keep flawless, and the shape naturally draws the eye down the length of the nail rather than across it.

Round and oval both work fine too, particularly when growing out longer square nails or coming from acrylics. The one shape to approach with caution is a long, dramatic stiletto point, since more length and a sharper tip mean more surface for a solid color to show any unevenness.

